  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nTotal amount = ₹ 4,760\n\n(9/16) of Rishi's amount = (3/4) of Sarita's amount\n\n**Formula Used:**\n\nLet Rishi's amount be x and Sarita's amount be ₹ 4,760 - x\n\n(9/16) × x = (3/4) × (4,760 - x)\n\n**Calculation:**\n\n⇒ (9/16) × x = (3/4) × (4,760 - x)\n\n⇒ (9/16) × x = (3/4) × 4,760 - (3/4) × x\n\n⇒ (9/16) × x + (3/4) × x = (3/4) × 4,760\n\n⇒ (9/16 + 3/4) × x = 3 × 1,190\n\n⇒ (9/16 + 12/16) × x = 3,570\n\n⇒ (21/16) × x = 3,570\n\n⇒ x = (3,570 × 16) / 21\n\n⇒ x = ₹ 2,720\n\nTherefore, Sarita's amount = ₹ 4,760 - ₹ 2,720 = 2040.\n\n**Sarita has ₹ 2,040.**\n\n42:T59b,<",
